# /sdd-analyze

Purpose:
  Analyze and explain the .sdd/ system structure. Read-only — does not
  modify any files. Performs integrated analysis across .sdd/ and .specdd/
  runtime artifacts.

Owns: commands\sdd-analyze.sdd

Description:
  Multi-mode system analysis command. Scans .sdd/ specifications,
  .specdd/ runtime artifacts, and knowledge health. Produces an integrated
  analysis report covering system health, knowledge integrity, and
  recommended next steps.

Usage:
  /sdd-analyze
  /sdd-analyze --chains
  /sdd-analyze --decisions
  /sdd-analyze --project
  /sdd-analyze --knowledge
  /sdd-analyze --specdd
  /sdd-analyze --all

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - the target area's INDEX only (chains/INDEX.sdd OR decisions/INDEX.sdd
    OR projects/sddra/INDEX.sdd, per focus flag)
  Deep specs load on EXPAND only — analysis goes layer by layer, not bulk.

Options:
  --chains     Focus on chain graph
  --decisions  Focus on decision ledger
  --project    Focus on project structure
  --knowledge  Focus on knowledge health (references, trust, lifecycle status)
  --specdd     Focus on .specdd/ runtime artifacts (flow-index, fix-index)
  --all        Full integrated analysis (default when no option specified)

ScanScope:
  sdd_specs:
    - @../INDEX.sdd
    - @../PROJECT.sdd
    - @../protocol/ROOT.sdd
    - @../architecture/INDEX.sdd
    - @../chains/graph.sdd
    - @../workflow/INDEX.sdd
    - @../tasks/tasks.sdd
    - @../commands/INDEX.sdd
 
  knowledge_system:
    - @../concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd
    - @../knowledge/KNOWLEDGE-LIFECYCLE.sdd
    - @../references/INDEX.sdd
    - @../knowledge/GOLDEN-RULES.sdd
    - @../lessons/REJECTED-APPROACHES.sdd
    - trust metadata validation
    - lifecycle status (OBSERVED -> CANDIDATE -> VALIDATED -> ESTABLISHED)
    - evidence type coverage (CODE, TEST, TASK, DECISION, PROJECT,
      PRODUCTION, EXTERNAL, HUMAN)
    - orphaned or stale knowledge entries
    - duplicate concepts detection

  specdd_artifacts:
    - .specdd/flow-index.md (CASE dependency tree: depends-on, related)
    - .specdd/fix-index.sdd (problem -> fix lookup table)
    - .specdd/dependency-ledger.md (security and dependency state)
    - .specdd/task-context/ (per-task context artifacts)
    - fix-index integrity (entries are linked, not orphaned)
    - flow-index acyclicity (depends-on tree has no cycles)
    - dependency-ledger currency (no unresolved security findings)

   runtime_state:
     - @../runtime/memory-model.sdd (4-tier memory health)
     - @../runtime/context-builder.sdd (context loading completeness)
     - context budget utilization (current level vs. allowed levels)
     - @../runtime/mcp-integration.sdd (MCP server security profile)

  sdd_methodology:
     - @../references/sdd/INDEX.sdd (SDD best practices and tool landscape)
     - @../references/sdd/best-practices.sdd (Three Levels, Core Workflow, EARS)
     - @../references/sdd/tool-comparison.sdd (Cosmos, Kiro, Spec Kit, etc.)
     - @../references/sdd/ecc-framework-overview.sdd (ECC framework summary)
     - @../references/sdd/living-specs-best-practices.sdd (living spec patterns)
     - @../agent/ecc-bridge.sdd (ECC agent ? SDD role mapping)

  evolution_health:
     - @../timeline/INDEX.sdd (temporal knowledge system)
     - @../evolution/INDEX.sdd (candidate pool, discovery)
     - @../policies/evolution.sdd (approval levels, evolution budget)
     - @../queries/INDEX.sdd (query language health)

  Output:
   Integrated analysis report containing:
     SystemOverview:
       - .sdd/ file count and header validity
       - Reference resolution health (broken @references)
       - Navigation consistency
       - SDD specification health (State: + markers, Navigation sections)

     KnowledgeHealth:
       - Reference count by status (OBSERVED, CANDIDATE, VALIDATED, ESTABLISHED, DEPRECATED)
       - Trust distribution across knowledge hierarchy
       - Evidence coverage ratio (entries with evidence / total entries)
       - Stale entries (older than 30 days without status change)
       - Orphaned concepts (no @reference links)
       - Duplicate concepts (same-as conflicts)
       - Knowledge gaps (CANDIDATE aging without promotion)

     SpecDDAnalysis:
       - Flow index: open vs. completed CASE dependencies
       - Fix index: coverage count, last-updated entries, recurrence patterns
       - Dependency ledger: open vs. resolved CVEs, remediation status
       - Task context: loaded vs. missing context per active task

     SDDMethodologyHealth:
       - SDD reference coverage (best practices, tool comparison, ECC overview)
       - Living spec status (auto-updating vs static)
       - Spec drift detection (references vs implementation)

     EvolutionHealth:
       - Evolution budget utilization
       - Pending challenges and proposals
       - Timeline integrity (change records, snapshots, migrations)

     IntegratedFindings:
       - Cross-artifact conflicts (e.g. flow-index references non-existent CASE)
       - Knowledge-to-code traceability gaps
       - SDD specification gaps (missing State: +, missing Navigation)
       - ECC integration coverage gaps
       - Recommended next actions prioritized by risk

     RecommendedNextSteps:
       - Prioritized action list with rationale
       - Risk and effort estimates per action

  Rules:
   [A1] /sdd-analyze MUST NOT modify any file — read-only operation.
   [A2] /sdd-analyze MUST resolve all @references before reporting broken links.
   [A3] /sdd-analyze MUST scan .specdd/ artifacts when --specdd or --all is used.
   [A4] /sdd-analyze MUST validate flow-index acyclicity when --specdd is used.
   [A5] /sdd-analyze MUST cross-reference fix-index with open tasks when --all is used.
   [A6] /sdd-analyze MUST NOT expose secrets or credentials in output.
   [A7] /sdd-analyze MUST report knowledge health metrics when --knowledge or --all is used.
   [A8] /sdd-analyze MUST flag stale knowledge entries (>30 days without promotion).
   [A9] /sdd-analyze output format is structured text — suitable for both human and AI consumption.
   [A10] /sdd-analyze MUST report broken @references even in partial (--chains, --decisions) mode.
   [A11] /sdd-analyze MUST report SDD specification health (State: + markers, Navigation sections).
   [A12] /sdd-analyze MUST detect spec drift against ECC tool landscape references.

State: +
   (extended to scan .specdd/ runtime artifacts and knowledge health per PHASE 120-124)
   (integrated analysis output covering .sdd/ specs, .specdd/ runtime, and knowledge system)